factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The article says the children came from special schools across Tamil Nadu, but the reel_script and caption say 'தமிழ்நாடு முழுவதும்' was the source only for 'அரசு சிறப்புப் பள்ளிகள்' — this matches; however, the reel_script and caption say the 250 children came from the listed districts, while the article says the 250 were from schools across Tamil Nadu and only the participants from Kanchipuram, Virudhunagar, Tambaram and Poonamallee were named — the draft's wording merges these into one claim, which is a mixed-fact sentence.
  The reel_script says the trip began at the airport metro station and the article says the trip started from the airport metro station, but the reel_script omits the key fact that the children travelled from the airport station to the A.G.D.M.S. station in a single sentence that also attributes the trip to the metro company and commission, mixing distinct facts.
  The reel_script states the programme was held 'மெட்ரோ பயண அனுபவம் பெற' as a cause, but the article says the children gained the metro travel experience through the trip; the phrase 'இந்த நிகழ்ச்சி ஏற்படுத்தப்பட்டது' is grammatically unclear and presents an invented purpose.
  The slides_spec text 'ஆசிரியர்கள் மற்றும் மாணவர்கள் பயணம்' and reel_script 'மாணவர்கள் பங்கேற்றனர்' describe the children as students, while the article describes them as 'மாற்றுத்திறனாளி குழந்தைகள்' and the caption says 'பள்ளிகளின் மாணவர்கள்' — the reel_script and caption use 'மாணவர்கள்' which is not an inaccuracy but the caption 'பள்ளிகளின் மாணவர்கள் இணைந்தனர்' attributes the Kanchipuram/Virudhunagar/Tambaram/Poonamallee origin to all schools, an unsupported specific claim.
